<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns/1.0/graphml.xsd">
  <key id="d6" for="edge" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d5" for="edge" attr.name="keywords" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d4" for="edge" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d3" for="edge" attr.name="weight" attr.type="double" />
  <key id="d2" for="node" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d1" for="node" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d0" for="node" attr.name="entity_type" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;SCOTTISH JUDICIAL COMMUNITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Scottish Judicial Community includes judges, legal scholars, and advocates who are part of the Scottish legal system and are impacted by judicial reforms and social justice issues."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0411</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LORD KENNET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lord Kennet is a respected Scottish judge and legal scholar who has been involved in high-profile cases and is known for his advocacy of judicial reform and social justice."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0411</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EMMA WOOD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Emma Wood is a well-known society matron and philanthropist who has been married to Sir Nicholas Brooksbank for over 40 years and is now married to Lord Kennet."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0411</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ROBERT BRUCE, LORD KENNET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Robert Bruce, Lord Kennet is a Scottish judge and legal scholar who has been involved in high-profile cases and is known for his advocacy of judicial reform and social justice."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0411</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SIR NICHOLAS BROOKSBANK, 3RD BARONET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sir Nicholas Brooksbank, 3rd Baronet is the husband of Emma Wood and a notable figure in Scottish society."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0411</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LADY MARGARET MACPHERSON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lady Margaret Macpherson is a longtime friend of Lord Kennet and Emma Wood and is known for her comments on their relationship."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0411</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DALHOUSIE CASTLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dalhousie Castle is the site of Lord Kennet and Emma Wood's private wedding ceremony."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0411</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MIDLOTHIAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Midlothian is the county where Dalhousie Castle is located and where the wedding ceremony took place."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0411</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIGH-PROFILE CASES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"High-profile cases refer to significant legal cases that Lord Kennet has presided over and are of great public interest."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0411</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JUDICIAL REFORM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Judicial Reform is an ongoing effort to improve the Scottish legal system, which Lord Kennet has advocated for."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0411</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOCIAL JUSTICE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Social Justice is a cause that Lord Kennet has supported and is expected to continue supporting with his new wife."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0411</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HELEN ABERCROMBY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Helen Abercromby was the first wife of Lord Kennet, who died in 1786."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0411</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EDINBURGH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Edinburgh is the capital city of Scotland and the location where the news of Lord Kennet's marriage was reported."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0411</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COURT OF SESSION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Court of Session is Scotland's highest civil court, where Lord Kennet served as a judge."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0411</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SCOTTISH ADVOCATES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Scottish Advocates are lawyers who practice in the Scottish legal system, of which Lord Kennet is a prominent member."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0411</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LEGAL SCHOLARS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Legal Scholars are experts in the field of law, of which Lord Kennet is a respected member."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0411</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHILANTHROPISTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Philanthropists are individuals who engage in charitable activities, of which Emma Wood is a well-known member."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0411</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOCIETY MATRONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Society Matrons are influential women in society, of which Emma Wood is a well-known member."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0411</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SCOTTISH COURTS AND TRIBUNALS SERVICE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Scottish Courts and Tribunals Service provides support and resources to the Scottish legal system, of which Lord Kennet is a prominent figure."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0411</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PUBLIC SERVICE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Public Service is a commitment to serving the community, which both Lord Kennet and Emma Wood share."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0411</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LONGTIME FRIENDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Longtime Friends are individuals who have known each other for a long time, of which Lady Margaret Macpherson is a longtime friend of Lord Kennet and Emma Wood."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0411</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LORD KENNET, EMMA WOOD&quot;">
      <data key="d2">cb-0411</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lady Margaret Macpherson is a friend of Lord Kennet and Emma Wood and supports their union."</data>
      <data key="d0">"UNKNOWN"</data>
    </node>
    <edge source="&quot;SCOTTISH JUDICIAL COMMUNITY&quot;" target="&quot;LORD KENNET&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Lord Kennet is a prominent figure in the Scottish Judicial Community, known for his advocacy of judicial reform and social justice."</data>
      <data key="d5">"leadership, advocacy"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0411</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LORD KENNET&quot;" target="&quot;EMMA WOOD&quot;">
      <data key="d3">20.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Lord Kennet and Emma Wood have recently married, marking a significant personal and professional milestone for both individuals."</data>
      <data key="d5">"personal and professional partnership, judicial reform, social justice"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0411</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LORD KENNET&quot;" target="&quot;HIGH-PROFILE CASES&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Lord Kennet has presided over many high-profile cases, showcasing his expertise and fairness in the Scottish legal system."</data>
      <data key="d5">"judicial experience, public recognition"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0411</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LORD KENNET&quot;" target="&quot;JUDICIAL REFORM&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Lord Kennet is a vocal advocate for judicial reform, contributing to discussions and efforts to improve the Scottish legal system."</data>
      <data key="d5">"advocacy, improvement"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0411</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LORD KENNET&quot;" target="&quot;SOCIAL JUSTICE&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Lord Kennet supports social justice causes, which he and his new wife are expected to continue advocating for together."</data>
      <data key="d5">"causes, partnership"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0411</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LORD KENNET&quot;" target="&quot;SCOTTISH ADVOCATES&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Lord Kennet is a prominent member of the Scottish Advocates, a group of lawyers who practice in the Scottish legal system."</data>
      <data key="d5">"professional affiliation, expertise"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0411</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LORD KENNET&quot;" target="&quot;LEGAL SCHOLARS&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Lord Kennet is a respected member of the Legal Scholars, a group of experts in the field of law."</data>
      <data key="d5">"scholarship, expertise"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0411</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LORD KENNET&quot;" target="&quot;COURT OF SESSION&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Lord Kennet served as a judge of the Court of Session, Scotland's highest civil court."</data>
      <data key="d5">"judicial experience, public recognition"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0411</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;EMMA WOOD&quot;" target="&quot;SIR NICHOLAS BROOKSBANK, 3RD BARONET&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Emma Wood is currently married to Sir Nicholas Brooksbank, 3rd Baronet, and is now also married to Lord Kennet."</data>
      <data key="d5">"divorce, remarriage"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0411</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;EMMA WOOD&quot;" target="&quot;PHILANTHROPISTS&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Emma Wood is a well-known member of the Philanthropists, a group of individuals who engage in charitable activities."</data>
      <data key="d5">"charitable work, influence"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0411</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;EMMA WOOD&quot;" target="&quot;SOCIETY MATRONS&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Emma Wood is a well-known Society Matron, an influential woman in society."</data>
      <data key="d5">"influence, societal role"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0411</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LADY MARGARET MACPHERSON&quot;" target="&quot;LORD KENNET, EMMA WOOD&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Lady Margaret Macpherson is a friend of Lord Kennet and Emma Wood and supports their union."</data>
      <data key="d5">"friendship, support"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0411</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;DALHOUSIE CASTLE&quot;" target="&quot;LORD KENNET, EMMA WOOD&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Lord Kennet and Emma Wood held their private wedding ceremony at Dalhousie Castle, an intimate setting for their union."</data>
      <data key="d5">"ceremony location, intimacy"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0411</data>
    </edge>
